<main>
  <span class="badge">In development</span>
  <h1>Spore Wars</h1>
  <p class="tagline prose">A vertical-scrolling shoot-'em-up in the mid-90s PC style. Climb five gun levels, buy shields and upgrades with salvaged cores, and face a boss every fifth wave.</p>

  <figure class="hero" style="display:block; max-width:960px">
    <img src="../assets/spore-wars/hangar.png" width="960" height="540" alt="The player's starfighter parked in a hangar bay, a blue planet seen through the doors">
  </figure>

  <!-- PLAY LINKS. When the game goes live on a portal, replace the href and
       remove aria-disabled. Keep every live portal listed; players may prefer one. -->
  <div class="box">
    <h2>Play</h2>
    <p>Spore Wars will be free to play in the browser on game portals. Nothing to install.</p>
    <p>
      <a class="btn" href="#" aria-disabled="true">&#9654; Play on itch.io &mdash; coming soon</a>
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">Planned rollout: itch.io first, then CrazyGames and Poki. Links appear here as each goes live.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Screenshots</h2>
  <p class="prose">Captured from the current development build. Three sectors, a boss every fifth wave, and a salvage trader between sectors.</p>
  <div class="gallery">
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-1-foundry.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="Fighting through the Orbital Foundry: the player ship fires blue pulse bolts up a steel canyon at a diving alien"><figcaption>Wave 1, Orbital Foundry</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-2-chain.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="A kill chain building to x2 as a wave of scouts breaks apart above the player ship"><figcaption>Kill chains raise the score multiplier</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-3-battleship.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="The Battleship boss fills the top of the screen, turrets raining red shots while its health bar drains"><figcaption>Wave 5: the Battleship</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-4-salvage.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="Infected Salvage sector: purple overgrown wreckage, a tentacled lurker spitting green spore shots"><figcaption>Infected Salvage: the machines are changing</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-5-mech.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="The Assault Mech boss locks its aim on the player while green spore rounds curve in"><figcaption>Wave 10: the Assault Mech</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-6-heart.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="Spore Heart sector: a biological cavern of ribbed tissue, the twin gun firing at spore skimmers"><figcaption>Spore Heart: beyond the last machine</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-7-broodmother.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="The Brood Mother spreads across the top of the screen; the game says to destroy her launch bays"><figcaption>Wave 15: the Brood Mother</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="../assets/spore-wars/shot-8-trader.webp" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="The Salvage Exchange: an alien trader behind a counter offering permanent upgrades for cores"><figcaption>Between sectors: spend cores at the Salvage Exchange</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2>Readme</h2>
  <dl class="spec">
    <dt>Genre</dt><dd>Vertical shoot-'em-up, endless waves with upgrades</dd>
    <dt>Platform</dt><dd>Browser (desktop and phone), keyboard or touch</dd>
    <dt>Price</dt><dd>Free, supported by portal ads</dd>
    <dt>Status</dt><dd>In development. First release on itch.io.</dd>
    <dt>Made with</dt><dd>Plain HTML5 Canvas and JavaScript, no engine</dd>
  </dl>

  <div class="prose">
    <h3>What's in it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Five weapon levels with distinct hardware, homing support rockets at level four, and a megabomb for emergencies</li>
      <li>A three-hit hull, shields, repair pickups and a kill-chain score multiplier</li>
      <li>Three sectors, from the Orbital Foundry through Infected Salvage to the Spore Heart</li>
      <li>Rotating bosses every fifth wave: the Battleship, the Assault Mech and the Brood Mother</li>
      <li>Cores salvaged in combat buy permanent upgrades from an alien trader between sectors</li>
      <li>Sound effects synthesised to sound like an early-90s sound card, and a CC0 music loop that shifts with each sector</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
  <p class="prose">Spore Wars uses openly licensed art and music from other creators. Full attributions, with the changes we made, are below. The same text ships inside the game. Studio-wide licence notes are on the <a href="../credits.html">credits page</a>.</p>

  <!-- Mirrors CREDITS.txt in the spore-wars repo. Keep the two in step. -->
  <h3>Art</h3>
  <ul class="credits">
    <li>
      <span class="what">Player ship, alien fleet, bosses and mechs</span><br>
      "Space Ship Construction Kit" and "Space Ship / Mech Construction Kit 2" by Skorpio<br>
      <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/space-ship-construction-kit">opengameart.org/content/space-ship-construction-kit</a><br>
      <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/space-ship-mech-construction-kit-2">opengameart.org/content/space-ship-mech-construction-kit-2</a><br>
      <span class="lic">Licence: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC-BY-SA 3.0</a>. Modified: cropped, resized, palette-reduced, recoloured and outlined by 640K Games. The modified ship and alien sprites are released under the same CC-BY-SA 3.0 licence.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">Legacy weapon bolts, plasma, pickup icons, fireball flashes</span><br>
      "Remastered Tyrian Graphics" by Daniel Cook (Lostgarden.com)<br>
      <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/remastered-tyrian-graphics">opengameart.org/content/remastered-tyrian-graphics</a><br>
      <span class="lic">Licence: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/">CC-BY 3.0</a>. Modified: individual sprites extracted, upscaled and palette-reduced.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">Explosions, hit sparks, muzzle flash, smoke</span><br>
      "explosions" by chabull<br>
      <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/explosions-0">opengameart.org/content/explosions-0</a><br>
      <span class="lic">Licence: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/">CC-BY 3.0</a>. Modified: frames selected, resized, alpha dithered and palette-reduced.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">Space background (retained as a fallback)</span><br>
      "Parallax Space Scene" by LuminousDragonGames<br>
      <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/parallax-space-scene-seamlessly-scrolls-too">opengameart.org/content/parallax-space-scene-seamlessly-scrolls-too</a><br>
      <span class="lic">Licence: CC0. Modified: resized, palette-reduced, alpha dithered.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">UI icons and particles (reserved)</span><br>
      Kenney, <a href="https://www.kenney.nl">kenney.nl</a><br>
      <span class="lic">Licence: CC0.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">AI-assisted illustrations</span><br>
      The title-menu hangar (the picture above), the three sector backdrops, the Battleship hull, the Mech and Brood Mother bodies, the crawler, lurker and spore skimmer, the ground sentries and the salvage trader are AI-assisted: generated with OpenAI image generation under 640K Games' art direction, then edited, encoded and composed by 640K Games. No third-party source pack used. Animation, interface and effects are drawn by the game code. Everything else in the game is human-made.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">Studio logo and bitmap font</span><br>
      The 640K Games wordmark, icon and the in-game alphabet extended from its letterforms are original studio artwork, &copy; 640K Games, not covered by the Creative Commons licences above.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="what">Player weapon bolts, gun mounts and muzzle flashes</span><br>
      Original procedural artwork by 640K Games, generated by the game code.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Music</h3>
  <ul class="credits">
    <li>
      <span class="what">Main theme: "Space Adventure"</span> by MintoDog<br>
      <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/space-adventure">opengameart.org/content/space-adventure</a><br>
